  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia-Indonesia Health Security Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia-Indonesia Health Security Partnership (AIHSP) is focused on strengthening Indonesia&apos;s capacity to prevent, detect, and respond to health emergencies. This partnership works to mitigate the threat posed by emerging infectious diseases, including COVID-19, and zoonoses&#x2014;diseases transmitted between animals and humans. Operating in five Indonesian provinces (Central Java, Yogyakarta, Bali, South Sulawesi, and East Nusa Tenggara), AIHSP aims to bolster Indonesia&#x2019;s national health security, protecting individuals and communities by reducing the risks and impacts of these diseases.</narrative>
  </description>
